# Action-first navigation

User actions and route changes must feel instant. Never block UI on DB/API when an optimistic path exists.

## Navigation

- Sidebar links use `NavLink` (`src/components/layout/nav-link.tsx`) with `useTransition`.
- Global `src/app/loading.tsx` shows skeleton while server pages load.
- Screener form uses `startTransition` + `router.push` — navigate first, server re-renders after.

## Mutations (optimistic pattern)

```tsx
// 1. Apply local state change immediately
setItems(next);
setModalOpen(false);

// 2. Sync in background
void syncToServer(next).then((ok) => {
  if (!ok) {
    setItems(prev); // rollback
    setError("Save failed");
    return;
  }
  router.refresh(); // optional background reconcile
});
```

Apply to: watchlist toggles, holdings ledger, trading ledger, strategy save, sign-out.

## Do not

- `await` DB/server action before updating visible UI state on toggles and saves
- Disable nav links while a page is loading (show pending indicator instead)
- Block `router.push` until `router.refresh` completes

## Server pages

Server pages may still fetch DB on first paint — that is fine. The shell (sidebar + loading skeleton) must appear immediately on navigation.
